            "type": "TextBlock",
            "size": "Large",
            "weight": "Bolder",
            "text": "The NFA story moves to the states: 15 states still make suppressors and short-barreled guns legal only if they're federally registered.",
            "wrap": true,
            "spacing": "Small"
          },
          {
            "type": "TextBlock",
            "text": "FPC asked the attorneys general of 15 states to stop enforcing state laws tied to federal NFA registration. ATF's pause does not override state law, so members there could skip federal paperwork and still face state charges.",
            "wrap": true,
            "spacing": "Small"
          },
